# Is a tomato a fruit?
subtitle: "Pick out the fruits among six salad and soup foods the way a botanist would, and learn what makes a fruit a fruit."
tags: ["botany","fruit classification","tomatoes","plant biology","vegetables"]
teaches: ["vocabulary/fruit-definition","concepts/botanical-vs-culinary-classification","methods/plant-identification"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Laomedeia | an upbeat, playful quiz host who loves a botanical surprise; light and quick","take":"lines"}

## Is a tomato a fruit?
sources:
    - id: britannica
      title: Fruit (plant reproductive body)
      authors: Encyclopaedia Britannica
      year: 2024
      url: https://www.britannica.com/science/fruit-plant-reproductive-body
      finding: a fruit is the ripened ovary of a flowering plant, enclosing the seed or seeds
    - id: nix
      title: Nix v. Hedden, 149 U.S. 304
      authors: Supreme Court of the United States
      year: 1893
      url: https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/149/304/
      finding: tomatoes are vegetables for the purposes of the Tariff Act of 1883

Is a tomato a fruit? To a botanist, a fruit is the part of a flowering plant that grows from the flower and holds the seeds.
    cards food cites ["britannica","nix"] select Fruits
        * "Tomato" icon tomato in true
        * "Cucumber" icon cucumber in true
        * "Chili" icon "hot pepper" in true
        * "Carrot" icon carrot in false
        * "Potato" icon potato in false
        * "Broccoli" icon broccoli in false

    ask "Which of these are fruits, the way a botanist sees it? Tap every fruit." on food store f feedback.style dry feedback.reward auto feedback.perfect "Suspiciously good. Are you a botanist?" feedback.good "Nearly all of them. The greengrocer would hire you." feedback.poor "Don't worry: the greengrocer gets these wrong too." feedback.none "Bold. Wrong, but bold. Botany is not on your side today."
        right: All {f.total} right.
        wrong: {f} of {f.total} on the first try.

Tomatoes, cucumbers and chilies all grow from a flower and carry their seeds inside, so to a botanist they are fruits.
    highlight food_bin_1

Carrots, on the other hand, are roots, potatoes are swollen underground stems, and broccoli is a bunch of flower buds that have not opened yet.
    highlight food_4 food_5 food_6

The kitchen still calls the tomato a vegetable, and in 1893 the US Supreme Court agreed, for the sake of import taxes.
    highlight food_1
